1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,307
Imagine waking up one morning to discover that the world has changed.

2
00:00:04,481 --> 00:00:05,886
A man has appeared.

3
00:00:06,060 --> 00:00:11,250
He travels across the earth, attracting enormous crowds wherever he goes.

4
00:00:11,424 --> 00:00:17,253
He promises people wealth, food, rain, and things they never thought possible.

5
00:00:17,578 --> 00:00:21,897
Some people begin following him because they believe he has come to save them.

6
00:00:22,175 --> 00:00:27,655
Others follow him because they are terrified of what might happen if they refuse.

7
00:00:28,038 --> 00:00:31,057
But there is one thing they don't understand.

8
00:00:31,440 --> 00:00:34,134
This man is not a savior.

9
00:00:34,377 --> 00:00:38,348
He is the greatest deceiver humanity will ever face.

10
00:00:38,511 --> 00:00:43,387
In Islamic tradition, he is known as Al-Masih Ad-Dajjal.

11
00:00:43,526 --> 00:00:45,001
The false messiah.

12
00:00:45,302 --> 00:00:48,890
The Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him,

13
00:00:49,018 --> 00:00:51,653
warned his followers about him repeatedly.

14
00:00:51,886 --> 00:00:57,482
In fact, no prophet was sent without warning his people about this dangerous trial.

15
00:00:57,691 --> 00:01:00,419
But who exactly is Dajjal?

16
00:01:00,593 --> 00:01:01,951
What will he look like?

17
00:01:02,102 --> 00:01:04,262
What powers will he appear to have?

18
00:01:04,540 --> 00:01:09,590
And most importantly, how can Muslims protect themselves from his deception?

19
00:01:09,869 --> 00:01:13,619
To understand the answer, we need to look at what the Prophet,

20
00:01:13,689 --> 00:01:17,636
peace and blessings be upon him, actually taught us.

21
00:01:18,449 --> 00:01:19,447
Chapter one.

22
00:01:20,144 --> 00:01:21,433
Who is Dajjal?

23
00:01:21,874 --> 00:01:26,611
The word Dajjal is associated with deception and concealment.

24
00:01:26,936 --> 00:01:33,670
In Islamic belief, Al-Masih Ad-Dajjal is a real individual who will appear before the Day of

25
00:01:33,763 --> 00:01:34,563
Judgment.

26
00:01:34,750 --> 00:01:40,439
He will be a liar who claims extraordinary things and tests the faith of humanity.

27
00:01:40,822 --> 00:01:44,084
His trial is so serious that the Prophet Muhammad,

28
00:01:44,293 --> 00:01:49,193
peace and blessings be upon him, warned his companions about him.

29
00:01:49,797 --> 00:01:54,278
In Sahih Muslim, the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him,

30
00:01:54,522 --> 00:02:00,176
explained that every prophet before him had warned their people about the Dajjal.

31
00:02:00,989 --> 00:02:05,331
Even Prophet Nuh, peace be upon him, warned his people.

32
00:02:06,260 --> 00:02:07,386
Think about that.

33
00:02:07,711 --> 00:02:12,959
Generation after generation, prophets warned humanity about this coming trial.

34
00:02:13,330 --> 00:02:17,255
And the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him,

35
00:02:17,429 --> 00:02:20,204
made sure his Ummah understood the danger.

36
00:02:20,447 --> 00:02:23,768
This isn't simply a story about a frightening person.

37
00:02:24,151 --> 00:02:29,689
It is a warning about how easily people can be deceived when their faith is weak.

38
00:02:30,804 --> 00:02:31,756
Chapter two.

39
00:02:32,870 --> 00:02:34,612
What will Dajjal look like?

40
00:02:35,216 --> 00:02:42,530
The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, gave specific descriptions of Dajjal so believers would

41
00:02:42,576 --> 00:02:43,598
recognize him.

42
00:02:44,190 --> 00:02:49,740
One of his most important characteristics is that he will be blind in one eye.

43
00:02:50,436 --> 00:02:56,253
The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, explained that Allah is not one-eyed.

44
00:02:56,636 --> 00:02:59,446
This distinction is extremely important.

45
00:03:00,142 --> 00:03:05,622
Dajjal will attempt to deceive people into believing that he possesses divine powers.

46
00:03:06,005 --> 00:03:11,648
But Allah, the Creator of everything, is far above any imperfection.

47
00:03:12,461 --> 00:03:19,682
Another description mentioned in authentic narrations is that the word Kafir will be written between Dajjal's

48
00:03:19,763 --> 00:03:20,563
eyes.

49
00:03:20,692 --> 00:03:27,251
The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, explained that believers would be able to recognize

50
00:03:27,298 --> 00:03:28,145
this writing.

51
00:03:28,749 --> 00:03:32,627
These descriptions are not given to satisfy curiosity.

52
00:03:32,836 --> 00:03:34,055
They are warnings.

53
00:03:34,380 --> 00:03:41,125
The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, wanted his followers to recognize the deception rather

54
00:03:41,183 --> 00:03:43,285
than be fooled by appearances.

55
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:45,456
Chapter three.

56
00:03:45,839 --> 00:03:48,243
The powers that will test humanity.

57
00:03:48,672 --> 00:03:52,399
Now comes one of the most frightening parts of the narrations.

58
00:03:52,712 --> 00:03:58,285
Dajjal will be given extraordinary abilities that will test people's faith.

59
00:03:58,773 --> 00:04:03,509
In Sahih Muslim, the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him,

60
00:04:03,835 --> 00:04:08,978
described how Dajjal will come with something resembling Paradise and Hellfire.

61
00:04:09,361 --> 00:04:11,323
But there is a terrifying twist.

62
00:04:11,764 --> 00:04:15,270
What he presents as Paradise will actually be Hellfire.

63
00:04:15,595 --> 00:04:19,670
And what he presents as Hellfire will actually be Paradise.

64
00:04:19,914 --> 00:04:24,999
Imagine being placed in a situation where everything appears completely backwards.

65
00:04:25,510 --> 00:04:28,308
Something that looks beautiful may be a trap.

66
00:04:28,633 --> 00:04:32,824
Something that looks frightening may actually be the path to safety.

67
00:04:33,335 --> 00:04:36,597
This is why the trial of Dajjal is so dangerous.

68
00:04:37,108 --> 00:04:43,784
People may begin judging truth by what looks attractive rather than by what Allah has revealed.

69
00:04:44,596 --> 00:04:50,982
The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, also described how Dajjal will appear to have

70
00:04:51,040 --> 00:04:54,233
control over rain and the growth of crops.

71
00:04:54,836 --> 00:04:59,353
Some people will follow him and experience what appears to be prosperity.

72
00:04:59,794 --> 00:05:02,824
Others will reject him and face hardship.

73
00:05:03,207 --> 00:05:09,186
His trial will test whether people remain faithful to Allah when the world seems to reward

74
00:05:09,244 --> 00:05:10,846
those who follow falsehood.

75
00:05:11,195 --> 00:05:13,064
But remember something important.

76
00:05:13,308 --> 00:05:16,791
These events will not make Dajjal equal to Allah.

77
00:05:16,941 --> 00:05:18,671
He is a creation of Allah.

78
00:05:18,892 --> 00:05:23,211
Whatever happens will only happen by Allah's permission.

79
00:05:23,838 --> 00:05:24,825
Chapter four.

80
00:05:25,069 --> 00:05:27,402
The forty days of Dajjal.

81
00:05:28,354 --> 00:05:33,312
One of the most fascinating details comes from a narration in Sahih Muslim.

82
00:05:33,695 --> 00:05:39,697
The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, explained that Dajjal will remain on earth for

83
00:05:39,767 --> 00:05:40,777
forty days.

84
00:05:40,893 --> 00:05:43,447
But these will not be ordinary days.

85
00:05:43,563 --> 00:05:45,746
The first day will be like a year.

86
00:05:45,897 --> 00:05:48,033
The second day will be like a month.

87
00:05:48,149 --> 00:05:50,332
The third day will be like a week.

88
00:05:50,425 --> 00:05:53,676
And the remaining days will be like normal days.

89
00:05:53,919 --> 00:05:55,986
The companions were confused.

90
00:05:56,137 --> 00:05:59,434
They asked the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him,

91
00:05:59,527 --> 00:06:04,728
whether the prayers of one day would be enough for a day lasting an entire year.

92
00:06:05,053 --> 00:06:06,493
His answer was no.

93
00:06:06,876 --> 00:06:12,205
Instead, Muslims would have to estimate the time and continue performing their prayers.

94
00:06:12,809 --> 00:06:15,560
Think about the importance of this instruction.

95
00:06:15,943 --> 00:06:21,330
Even during an extraordinary and frightening period, Salah would remain essential.

96
00:06:21,841 --> 00:06:28,447
The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, also explained that Dajjal would travel across the

97
00:06:28,540 --> 00:06:33,068
earth with incredible speed, like a cloud driven by the wind.

98
00:06:33,219 --> 00:06:35,622
His influence would spread rapidly.

99
00:06:35,866 --> 00:06:39,627
This is why the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him,

100
00:06:39,802 --> 00:06:43,401
warned believers not to underestimate his trial.

101
00:06:43,842 --> 00:06:45,107
Chapter five.

102
00:06:45,548 --> 00:06:47,719
Two cities he cannot enter.

103
00:06:48,230 --> 00:06:51,795
There is something else mentioned in the authentic narrations.

104
00:06:52,108 --> 00:06:57,634
Dajjal will travel through many places, but there are two cities he will not be able

105
00:06:57,669 --> 00:06:58,469
to enter.

106
00:06:58,702 --> 00:07:00,537
Makkah and Madinah.

107
00:07:01,036 --> 00:07:07,259
The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, explained that angels will guard the entrances of

108
00:07:07,317 --> 00:07:08,293
these cities.

109
00:07:08,618 --> 00:07:11,427
Dajjal will be unable to enter them.

110
00:07:11,868 --> 00:07:17,000
In Sahih Muslim, we also learn that he will approach Madinah but will not be allowed

111
00:07:17,046 --> 00:07:19,229
to enter its protected areas.

112
00:07:19,670 --> 00:07:21,934
Imagine the significance of this.

113
00:07:22,375 --> 00:07:26,799
While the world is experiencing one of the greatest trials in human history,

114
00:07:27,182 --> 00:07:31,756
these two sacred cities will be protected from Dajjal's entry.

115
00:07:32,360 --> 00:07:34,833
This is one of the many details the Prophet,

116
00:07:34,868 --> 00:07:40,394
peace and blessings be upon him, gave his Ummah so they would understand the seriousness of

117
00:07:40,452 --> 00:07:41,451
what is coming.

118
00:07:42,147 --> 00:07:43,366
Chapter six.

119
00:07:43,540 --> 00:07:45,746
The return of Prophet Isa.

120
00:07:46,443 --> 00:07:50,355
But Dajjal's story does not end with him deceiving people.

121
00:07:50,529 --> 00:07:53,826
The authentic narrations describe what happens next.

122
00:07:54,035 --> 00:07:57,588
Prophet Isa, peace be upon him, will descend.

123
00:07:57,913 --> 00:08:02,220
In Sahih Muslim, the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him,

124
00:08:02,336 --> 00:08:06,598
described Isa descending near the eastern side of Damascus.

125
00:08:06,772 --> 00:08:09,941
He will join the believers and pursue Dajjal.

126
00:08:10,324 --> 00:08:15,572
Eventually, Isa will catch up with him at the gate of Ludd and kill him.

127
00:08:15,897 --> 00:08:21,284
The great deceiver who caused so much corruption will finally be defeated.

128
00:08:21,667 --> 00:08:24,605
Dajjal's deception will not last forever.

129
00:08:24,883 --> 00:08:27,333
And this reminds us of something powerful.

130
00:08:27,658 --> 00:08:33,324
No matter how powerful falsehood appears, Allah's plan will always prevail.

131
00:08:34,438 --> 00:08:35,344
Chapter seven.

132
00:08:35,785 --> 00:08:38,339
How to protect yourself from Dajjal.

133
00:08:38,943 --> 00:08:43,169
Now, this is perhaps the most important part of the entire video.

134
00:08:43,611 --> 00:08:48,603
What can Muslims do today to protect themselves from the trial of Dajjal?

135
00:08:49,299 --> 00:08:54,814
The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, did not simply warn his followers.

136
00:08:55,139 --> 00:08:58,053
He also taught them ways to seek protection.

137
00:08:58,657 --> 00:09:02,964
First, memorize the first ten verses of Surah Al-Kahf.

138
00:09:03,405 --> 00:09:07,817
In Sahih Muslim, the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him,

139
00:09:07,968 --> 00:09:13,935
taught that whoever memorizes the first ten verses of Surah Al-Kahf will be protected from the

140
00:09:13,993 --> 00:09:15,433
trial of Dajjal.

141
00:09:15,874 --> 00:09:19,601
This is something every Muslim should take seriously.

142
00:09:19,984 --> 00:09:25,778
Second, regularly seek Allah's protection from Dajjal in your prayers.

143
00:09:26,219 --> 00:09:32,628
The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, taught Muslims to seek refuge from four things

144
00:09:32,709 --> 00:09:34,660
before finishing their Salah.

145
00:09:35,043 --> 00:09:36,587
The punishment of Hell.

146
00:09:36,912 --> 00:09:38,677
The punishment of the grave.

147
00:09:39,002 --> 00:09:41,080
The trials of life and death.

148
00:09:41,254 --> 00:09:44,052
And the trial of Al-Masih Ad-Dajjal.

149
00:09:44,435 --> 00:09:46,908
Third, strengthen your faith.

150
00:09:47,233 --> 00:09:48,731
Learn about Allah.

151
00:09:49,010 --> 00:09:50,472
Understand your religion.

152
00:09:50,646 --> 00:09:51,912
Study the Quran.

153
00:09:52,156 --> 00:09:57,717
And do not allow wealth, power, or impressive displays to make you forget who your Creator

154
00:09:57,798 --> 00:09:58,460
is.

155
00:09:58,460 --> 00:10:04,346
Because the greatest protection against deception is sincere faith and guidance from Allah.

156
00:10:04,950 --> 00:10:09,071
There is a reason the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him,

157
00:10:09,280 --> 00:10:12,844
warned his Ummah about Dajjal so many times.

158
00:10:13,169 --> 00:10:17,813
His trial will not simply be about recognizing a particular person.

159
00:10:18,022 --> 00:10:24,547
It will be about remaining firm when everything around you is designed to make you question

160
00:10:24,617 --> 00:10:25,417
the truth.

161
00:10:25,743 --> 00:10:27,983
People may follow him because of wealth.

162
00:10:28,494 --> 00:10:30,770
Others may follow him because of fear.

163
00:10:30,944 --> 00:10:35,843
And some may follow him because they become convinced by what they see.

164
00:10:36,168 --> 00:10:38,293
But a believer remembers something.

165
00:10:38,734 --> 00:10:40,534
Allah is our Lord.

166
00:10:40,859 --> 00:10:42,659
Allah is the Creator.

167
00:10:43,030 --> 00:10:46,780
And nothing in this world can ever be compared to Him.

168
00:10:47,024 --> 00:10:52,190
So don't wait until the greatest trials arrive before strengthening your faith.

169
00:10:52,515 --> 00:10:55,023
Start learning your religion today.

170
00:10:55,337 --> 00:10:57,345
Memorize Surah Al-Kahf.

171
00:10:57,670 --> 00:10:59,075
Protect your prayers.

172
00:10:59,353 --> 00:11:04,311
And ask Allah to protect you from the trials of this life and the Hereafter.

173
00:11:04,636 --> 00:11:09,117
May Allah protect us and our families from the fitnah of Dajjal,

174
00:11:09,268 --> 00:11:14,528
keep our hearts firm upon Islam, and allow us to die as believers.

175
00:11:14,911 --> 00:11:15,711
Ameen.

176
00:11:15,897 --> 00:11:17,604
And Allah knows best.
